    "explanation": "To both parties: the cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 charged to the rider stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.60 in compensation, being 80 percent of that fee, with the remaining 20 percent retained as the platform's service fee. The ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION because that is the outcome the case produces; the rider's own charge is not refunded, so the filing party's claim is not supported.\n\nWhy the fee stands. Every limb of POL-NS-01 holds on this record. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event, tapped at 19:36:38 (EV-TRIP-02734). (b) The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02734) places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at that same second: arrived_at is 19:36:38, the first qualifying in-geofence fix is 19:36:38, and 48 qualifying fixes sit inside the radius, so the POL-NS-02 proximity test is met with room to spare. (c) The driver then held position continuously for 469 seconds, from 19:36:38 to 19:44:27, against the free waiting period of 180 seconds in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no_show_threshold_sec is unset, so no longer threshold applies). (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 19:44:30 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell had elapsed, with no boarding event. The fee is therefore legitimately chargeable.\n\nRider's claims, answered. (1) The rider's POL-NS-04 / POL-NS-11 claim is correctly stated but does not win the case. The locating message 'im at the pickup, cant see you' was sent at 19:37:18 and the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor logged an in-app call before cancelling, so limbs (a) and (b) of POL-NS-04 hold. Limb (c), however, cannot be run: EV-GPS-02734 carries no rider track at all (rider_fix_count 0). Under POL-NS-11 that makes limb (c) UNDECIDABLE — neither satisfied nor failed — so POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider. I record that the test could not be run, and I do not infer that the rider was elsewhere. The absent rider track is a gap in the platform's export; it does not impair the driver's trace for arrival or dwell and does not lower the confidence cap on a finding drawn from the driver's own track. (2) The rider's POL-GEN-03 argument — that a disposition leaving the present state stands leaves the rider paying SGD 4.50 for a trip that produced no boarding and no completed trip, so only a refund takes the charge off her — is rejected. Since POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, the fee is properly chargeable; the disposition of the fee is that it stands, and the payment this case produces is to the driver, which is what makes the emitted value DRIVER_COMPENSATION rather than NO_ACTION. (3) The rider does not contest, and the record does not permit contesting, the arrival and dwell arithmetic; that concession is accepted. (4) The rider's POL-NS-06 claim about the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02734-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT, impairment disclosed) is accepted as far as it goes: POL-NS-06(i) cannot run because it requires an advisory that is present and populated, and in any event there is one continuous in-geofence interval (run_count 1) with nothing to sum and no shortfall — dwell of 469 seconds against a 180 second minimum is a surplus of 289 seconds, not a deficit.\n\nDriver's claims, answered. (1) The POL-NS-01 / POL-NS-02 claim is accepted (above). (2) The POL-NS-06 claim is accepted: the derived shortfall is minus 289 seconds, i.e. no shortfall, and the clock runs from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, which coincides with the arrival marker to the second, so no POL-NS-05 correction moves the start. (3) The POL-NS-05 false-arrival claim is accepted: the marker was a BUTTON press at 19:36:38 at which the trace places the driver at the pickup (closest approach 0.157 m), not more than 300 m away and not moving at 15 km/h or above; no clock skew exceeds the 90 second threshold of POL-NS-08(a). No false-arrival referral arises, because the clause does not bite. (4) The POL-NS-03 claim is accepted: the driver's sustained stationary run is inside the 50 m radius, so POL-NS-02 is satisfied rather than yielded, and there is a single registered pickup point, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises. (5) The POL-NS-07 claim is accepted: POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so compensation is 80 percent of SGD 4.50 = SGD 3.60, the figure EV-FARE-02734 itself derives. The anti-farming check requires both limbs and trips neither: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2 divided by completed_trips_30d of 92 is about 0.022 (below 0.08). Only the fields POL-GEN-01 permits for this test were used. (6) The POL-NS-08(d) money-reconciliation claim is accepted: fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee of 4.50 equals the net figure of 4.50 read from the platform policy in force (resolution_rule), payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, so there is no ledger integrity defect. (7) The POL-NS-09 / POL-GEN-02 claim is accepted: no escalation trigger fires. The GPS artifact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 — 104 fixes, 100 percent coverage, max gap 0.0 s — so no deciding fact rests on evidence impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d); the counterparty dispute counters are both 0; no_show_disputes_30d is 0; the anti-farming check is untripped; and no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival or dwell.\n\nNo clause produces a referral here: POL-NS-05 does not fire, POL-NS-06 does not fire with a shortfall, and the reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW was correctly selected, so no driver-education item is recorded. No open question is referred; none is needed. The monetary effect is SGD 3.60, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the ruling executes automatically on issue subject to appeal under POL-GEN-04. Confidence is 0.95, sitting under the cap of 1.0 set by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts."
